Whether you are organising a 30-person board retreat or a 900-person congress, you will find a configuration that fits.

## Seven Hotels, One Destination

Ensana operates **seven hotels** rated from 3 to 5 stars with a combined total of **over 900 rooms**:

- **Nové Lázně** ★★★★★ — the flagship, with historic Roman Baths and King Edward VII's Royal Cabin
- **Centrální Lázně** ★★★★ — directly connected to the spa treatment centre
- **Hvězda** ★★★★ — an elegant Art Nouveau house with Café Imperial
- **Pacifik** ★★★★ — a centrally located grand hotel
- **Butterfly** ★★★★ — a modern villa-style hotel
- **Svoboda** ★★★ and **Vltava** ★★★ — comfortable options for larger groups

VIP guests and rank-and-file attendees can all be accommodated in one destination, everything within walking distance of the conference centre.

## Where Business Meets Wellbeing

What sets Mariánské Lázně apart from conventional conference destinations is what happens between meeting sessions. The town sits on more than 100 natural mineral springs, and Ensana's spa facilities allow delegates to experience treatments drawn from local healing resources — mineral baths, dry CO₂ baths, peat wraps and a wide range of massages.

The **Roman Baths** at Nové Lázně, dating from 1896, offer a spa experience set against breathtakingly beautiful historic surroundings. For a truly exclusive experience, a mineral bath in the **original Royal Cabin of King Edward VII** can be arranged for groups — in the very suite used by the British monarch.

Pools, saunas, fitness centres and beauty salons across the resort round out the wellness offering. The result: delegates return to their meetings refreshed, focused and in better spirits than when they left.

## Gastronomy Tailored to Your Event

Ensana's culinary team prepares bespoke catering for events of all sizes:

- Gala dinners and formal banquets in the Casino's historic halls
- Standing receptions and cocktail evenings
- Coffee breaks, live cooking shows, bartender shows
- Tastings of Czech wine, craft beer and local specialities
- Outdoor barbecues on the terrace or in the park

Every menu is prepared to the client's specifications — from black-tie multi-course dinners to relaxed garden parties.

## Teambuilding and Accompanying Programmes

The surrounding countryside and the town's facilities open up a rich range of accompanying programmes:

- **Golf** at Royal Golf Club Mariánské Lázně — an 18-hole course founded in 1905 by King Edward VII, plus a public 9-hole Chip & Putt
- **Tennis and padel** on outdoor and indoor courts
- **Cycling, hiking and nordic walking** through forested hills and along promenades
- **Disc golf** on a public 18-hole course
- **Pétanque** in the Arnika grounds by the Colonnade
- **Archery** with a professional instructor
- **Winter skiing** at the Mariánky resort with a gondola lift and evening sessions

E-bikes, scooters, nordic walking poles and disc golf equipment are all available for hire.

## A Cultural Town All Year Round

Mariánské Lázně is no sleepy resort. The cultural calendar includes the **Chopin Festival**, **Marienbad Film Festival**, **Jazz Spa**, **Book Spa** and concerts by the **West Bohemian Symphony Orchestra** in the Casino halls. The iconic **Singing Fountain** at the Colonnade plays daily from spring to autumn.

For delegates with a free afternoon, the region offers:

- **Kladská Nature Reserve** — pristine peatland landscape
- **Premonstratensian Monastery in Teplá** — a Baroque gem
- **Kynžvart Castle** — the summer residence of Prince Metternich
- **Loket Castle** — a medieval fortress with a summer amphitheatre
- **Bečov Castle** — home to the Reliquary of St Maurus, the second most precious treasure in the Czech Republic
- **Karlovy Vary and Františkovy Lázně** — neighbouring spa towns
- **Breweries in Chodová Planá and Plzeň** — the cradle of Pilsner beer

## How to Get Here

| From | Distance |
|------|----------|
| Karlovy Vary Airport | 50 km |
| Prague | 160 km |
| Nuremberg | 170 km |
| Munich | 280 km |
| Frankfurt | 410 km |
| Berlin | 420 km |
| Vienna | 420 km |

Direct train connections from Prague. For international groups, Karlovy Vary Airport (seasonal charters) or Prague and Munich serve as the main gateways.

## UNESCO Heritage, Modern Service

Mariánské Lázně is part of the **Great Spa Towns of Europe** UNESCO World Heritage Site — recognition of the exceptional value of a place where natural springs, architecture and a culture of wellbeing come together. Hosting an event here means offering your guests not just a hall, but a destination with authentic character and history.

Ensana's conference team takes care of everything from planning to execution — room layout, AV technology, catering, room block reservations and accompanying programmes.

